```js
export function solve(nums, target) {
  let lo = 0;
  let hi = nums.length;

  while (lo < hi) {
    const mid = lo + Math.floor((hi - lo) / 2);
    if (nums[mid] < target) {
      lo = mid + 1;
    } else {
      hi = mid;
    }
  }

  return lo < nums.length && nums[lo] === target ? lo : -1;
}
```

The invariant is that every index below lo contains a value less than target, and every index at or above hi contains a value greater than or equal to target. At termination, lo is the first possible matching index; the final equality check returns that index or -1, including for an empty array. This preserves the synchronous API and requires no dependencies or test changes.

